Subject: [PATCH] logging: identify NAT-PMP and PCP result failures without
 changing warning policy

Convert seven mapping/external-address result diagnostics, retaining their
complete text, original category/severity and the once-only warning then
Debug policy for repeated NOT_AUTHORIZED. Keep the existing result string
and expose numeric error_code. The wire uint8/uint16 domain fits the existing
int64 metadata key exactly; no registry, renderer or API additions.

Extend existing scripted Sock cases for PCP NO_RESOURCES and NAT-PMP unknown
external-address/mapping failures. Check actual JSON warning records, exact
messages and decoded numeric result codes while retaining original protocol
scripts and MappingError assertions. No real UDP packets or response changes.
The once-only authorization transition is not newly forced or claimed covered.

Shared eCash PCP/NAT-PMP owner. Source-only event lint/diff checks pass;
modified native cases NOT_COMPILED/NOT_RUN. Sealed381/current intake unchanged.

